> ## Guffin Sampling/Cache Logic Change Checklist

**Goal:** Ensure correctness & minimal performance impact.

**I. Design & Planning (Before Coding):**

*   [ ] **Problem Definition:** Clearly define the issue & expected improvement.
*   [ ] **Architecture Impact:** Identify affected modules (Session, Engine, Sampler).
*   [ ] **Contract Review:** Understand & document changes to ownership, lifetime, & data validity contracts.
*   [ ] **Performance Estimate:** Estimate potential end-to-end gain – is it worthwhile?

**II. Automated Correctness Checks (Mandatory):**

*   [ ] **Tensor Admission Tests:** `tests/tensor/tensor_tests.cpp` - Validate tensor shapes & properties.
*   [ ] **Metal Numerical Tests:** `tests/tensor/gemma3_metal_tests.cpp` - Verify numerical accuracy (F16 rounding).
*   [ ] **Lossless Sampling Tests:** `tests/engine/lossless_sampling_tests.cpp` - Confirm probability distribution preservation.
*   [ ] **Target Runtime Tests:** `tests/engine/gemma3_target_runtime_tests.cpp` - Validate KV cache wrap & callback handling.
*   [ ] **Code Style:** Ensure adherence to `ENGINE_PRINCIPLES.md` (explicit ownership, data flow).

**III. Actual-Chat Performance Measurements (Post-Correctness):**

*   [ ] **Representative Prompt:** Use a standard prompt set for benchmarking.
*   [ ] **Baseline Comparison:** Compare against existing Guffin behavior.
*   [ ] **Metrics:** Measure tokens/s, TTFT, first text latency, memory footprint.
*   [ ] **Reproducibility:** Ensure consistent results across runs & hardware.



**Note:**  Any changes impacting numerical stability or data flow *must* be accompanied by new or updated correctness tests. Document rejected design ideas in the retrospective.
